Description: aym-js website
 This package provides the static website of AYM·JS, a sound chip emulator
 written in plain JavaScript and based on the Web Audio API.
 .
 AYM·JS emulates the AY-3-8910 PSG (Programmable Sound Generator) and the
 YM2149 SSG (Software-Controlled Sound Generator), two venerable sound chips
 widely used in the home computers, arcade boards and game consoles of the
 1980s. The emulation runs entirely in the web browser, with no plugin and no
 server-side component.
 .
 The website hosts two interactive applications built on top of the emulator:
 AYM·Player, a music player for tunes converted from the YM file format, and
 AYM·Synth, a virtual synthesizer made of two emulated chips offering a
 six-voice polyphony driven through the Web MIDI protocol. It also provides
 the documentation of the emulated chips and the license terms of the project.
 .
 The site is generated with the Hugo static website generator and is served by
 Apache. Installing this package deploys the generated site under
 /var/www/html/public and the matching Apache configuration under /etc/apache2.
